From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Flush downstream before locking the pins when
 seeking.

dmo_seeking_SetPositions() took each output pin's flushing_cs before
sending BeginFlush downstream. The stream thread holds that lock while it
delivers a sample (IMemInputPin_Receive), and a renderer may block in
Receive until it is flushed: the seek then waits for the stream thread,
which waits for the renderer, which waits for the flush. SNK Heroines Tag
Team Frenzy (its own renderer, looping movies) hung right after START.

Send BeginFlush first, as the Windows parsers and Wine's other parsers
do: the renderer returns from Receive, the stream thread releases the
lock, and the seek goes on.
---
 dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c b/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/winedmo_quartz_parser.c
@@ -636,6 +636,11 @@
     for (i = 0; i < filter->source_count; ++i)
         WakeConditionVariable(&filter->sources[i]->queue_cv);
 
+    /* Flush downstream first: a stream thread holds its pin's flushing_cs during Receive, and
+     * a renderer may block in Receive until it is flushed (Windows parsers do the same). */
+    if (!(current_flags & AM_SEEKING_NoFlush))
+        dmo_parser_begin_downstream_flush(filter);
+
     /* Acquire per-pin flushing_cs to ensure no Receive is in progress. */
     for (i = 0; i < filter->source_count; ++i)
     {
@@ -643,9 +648,6 @@
             EnterCriticalSection(&filter->sources[i]->flushing_cs);
     }
 
-    if (!(current_flags & AM_SEEKING_NoFlush))
-        dmo_parser_begin_downstream_flush(filter);
-
     SourceSeekingImpl_SetPositions(iface, current, current_flags, stop, stop_flags);
 
     /* Perform the actual seek. */
